/* book exam traps: Using Euler's column formula for a plate. A plate supported along its sides buckles at a load set by its width b and k, not by its length. | Putting a instead of b in Ncr = kπ²D/b². b is the loaded edge, across the load; a enters only through k. | Assuming k = 4 for every plate. It is 4 only at whole-number aspect ratios or for long plates with both unloaded edges simply supported; a free edge gives 0.425. | Mixing sign conventions. The buckling equation here takes compression positive; the general plate equation takes tension positive. | Reporting Ncr in N/m as a stress. Divide by t for σcr. */
