/* book Worked example 2: Q: The stringers of the same panel cripple at 250 MPa. The panel is 1200 mm wide with 8 stringers. Find the effective width at failure and the failing load of the panel, ignoring column buckling between ribs.
   1. be = 1.90 × 1.5 × √(70,000/250) = 2.85 × 16.73 = 47.7 mm, less than the pitch, so the sheet is buckled.
   2. Ae = 200 + 47.7 × 1.5 = 271.5 mm².
   3. Load per stringer: 250 × 271.5 = 67,884 N = 67.9 kN.
   4. Panel: 8 × 67.9 = 543 kN.
   5. Check against the loaded skin: the whole cross-section is 8 × 200 + 1200 × 1.5 = 3,400 mm², so the average failing stress is 160 MPa, well below the 250 MPa in the stringers.
   Answer: be = 47.7 mm at failure; the panel fails at about 543 kN (67.9 kN per stringer). */
